1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,931
There were a husband and a wife who
married young. They were sure they

2
00:00:05,931 --> 00:00:07,540
would have children.

3
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:16,193
But one year passed. Then two. Then
five.

4
00:00:16,967 --> 00:00:19,927
They prayed. They waited.

5
00:00:21,133 --> 00:00:26,383
Then the doctor told them that in
Ethiopia, their chance of having a

6
00:00:26,383 --> 00:00:28,853
child was less than one percent.

7
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:36,954
Many people would have lost hope here.
But they asked: “Where else can we

8
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:37,467
try?”

9
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:45,872
The answer was far away: Israel. A new
country, new doctors, a new language.

10
00:00:45,872 --> 00:00:47,040
Four years.

11
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:51,700
And then… a baby was born.

12
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,440
That baby was me.

13
00:00:56,967 --> 00:01:03,470
My mother still says: “Other women
give birth in nine months. But I gave

14
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:05,367
birth in nine years.”

15
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:11,153
Then my little sister was born. Then
my little brother.

16
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:16,067
I was that one percent. We all are.

17
00:01:16,967 --> 00:01:23,654
If they tell you your chance is one
percent, remember: one percent is not

18
00:01:23,654 --> 00:01:25,487
zero. Never give up.
